{
  "scope": "Move only fixed service signal callbacks, atomic state and lifetime-owned wake pipes into the platform; restore forbid(unsafe_code) in reload-config/rpcd/ubusd. No arbitrary safe signal callback registration API.",
  "compatibility": [
    "The same libc signal registration keeps the existing signal mask/restart semantics.",
    "RPCD HUP/USR1 retain last-pending-action semantics; CHLD wakes child reaping without replacing the action.",
    "ubusd reload and stop flags remain independent; HUP reload occurs before stopping/client service.",
    "Pipe writer/reader remain nonblocking and CLOEXEC. Platform OnceLock owns both until exec/process exit; repeated installation reuses the same pipe. Handler writers cannot become stale through application drop.",
    "Wake writes preserve errno and original byte values (rpcd 1, ubusd 0); full pipes never block.",
    "reload SIGINT/TERM latch the existing cancellation AtomicBool; the engine keeps its injectable flag interface.",
    "RPCD delayed child environment cleanup now uses ProcessOwner::acquire/remove_var, rejecting a failed main-thread safety check instead of relying on an unchecked Rust2021 environment setter."
  ],
